# Supervisor chat

- If the supervisor’s wording, spelling, or grammar would change the meaning, **restate the intended meaning in one sentence** and use that meaning. Persist the mapping if it is a standing term.
- **More than one open question:** ask **one** question, wait for the answer, then the next. Do not batch questions.
- Same turn, write every grouping lock into `order-grouping-locks.md` and regenerate `order-grouping-progress.xlsx` via `scripts/write_order_grouping_progress.py`.

Standing terms:

- **commit and push** (git) = supervisor asks in chat → agent commits the local delta (respect `.gitignore`; skip debug/temp/run junk) and pushes to `origin/main`. Not scheduled; not automatic. Author via one-shot `git -c user.name` / `user.email` (**Areeb Yaqub** / `46938981+areebxi@users.noreply.github.com`) — do not rewrite global git config. Locked 2026-09-29.
- **today** (ship-by) = run date **or overdue**, **or blank ship-by** (treat as today — if it is in ShipStation awaiting_shipment, pull it today; locked 2026-09-24). Unparseable non-blank ship-by → unmatched. **Skip store `DTFOcean.co.uk WP`** (not processed here). **Future ship-by** is not skipped. **Hashim #037:** Shift 1 **order** volume **above 300** → separate process CSVs for today vs later dates; ≤300 → may mix. Do not dump overflow into Shift 2/3 as caps. Filename has **no** today/future slot.
- **order pool** = ShipStation `awaiting_shipment` **only**. No supervisor CSV/file (export has no tags).
- **batch** = one output CSV / pile (the filename stem). Fixed batches use `B80` / `B100` / …; leftover Graph piles use `B1`, `B2`, … (skipping reserved fixed-batch numbers). Packing PIN: `{B}-S{n}-{process_number} Item {item_number}` (batch+shift only from the filename). Leftover criteria for that run date: `database/order-grouping-sorter/leftover_batches/{YYYY-MM-DD}.csv` (same columns as fixed_batches; written each sorter run).
- **fixed batch** = batch with a locked `B` code: **`B10` / `B40` / `B50` / `B70` / `B80` / `B90` / `B100` / `B1000` / `B1050` / `B1080` / `B2300` / `B2400` / `B3100` / `B3500` / `B3600` / `B3700` / `B4000` / `B5000` / `B5080` / `B5500` / `B8000` / `B8050`** (same code every shift; shift is only `S{n}`). Former “named floor”. Row order in `fixed_batches.csv` = priority (first match wins; locked 2026-09-28: Dancing Queen → Glow → Stickers → International → products → t-shirts → iron-on → plain Packs → plain Uneek). **B100** = own ready-made FOTL short-sleeve **Warehouse Stock**; **B50** = same as B100 but **Supplier On Demand** (locked 2026-09-30; B50 only — no other On Demand twins). **Plain batch** = leftover plain piles numbered `B2000`, `B2100`, `B2200`, `B2500`, `B2600`, `B2700`, … in the order made.
- **process number** = the increment **inside** a batch (`-1`, `-2`, …). Colour 3+ groups first, then **50 units** per process number (same threshold as Packing PDF `_Part N`). Same customer order stays on one process number. Not a new batch file.
- **item number** = `Item {n}` (space, not hyphen) — line inside that process number.
- **shift** = Packing Input folder + filename field 1 (after optional fixed-batch prefix). **Testing:** every sorter `--run` writes **`1st Shift` / `S1`** (replaces those CSVs). **Production later:** 1st `--run` of the day → 1st, 2nd → 2nd, …. No 300/100/100 write caps. `RESEND` / `UNMATCHED` have no shift slot in the name; they land in **this run’s** folder.
- **Packs colour** = **later**. Do not guess Item 1 Colour. Do not dump mixed packs to unmatched. Packs still split on Areeb + Brand Name + Pack Size.- **Fawad** = process-name slot for ShipStation store **MAS Clothing**. More peel-off channels later. Amazon is **not** its own channel (`own`).
- **Definite match:** grouping never guesses. No definite match → process file **`UNMATCHED`**. Floor handles it this run; then investigate and tighten logic/catalog so the next run matches. Same customer order stays together.
- **Mixed P vs R** (printed `Customise` in one order) = majority printed **units** take that pile; **even → readymade**. Whole order stays together. Not unmatched. Locked 2026-09-17.
- **Personalised ready** = customised (P) piles only when ShipStation tag **`1004- Personalised Design-Ready-`** (exact; British spelling + space after `1004-`). Design is already on the floor. Without that tag → held this run (not written). Readymade / plain unaffected. Locked 2026-09-25.
- **Mixed supply-method** (Warehouse Stock / In House / On Demand in one order) = whole order **Supplier On Demand** (on-demand item arrives later). Not unmatched. Locked 2026-09-22.
- **Resend** = tag **`1014-ALL-RESEND` only**. Not 1015 / 1016 / 1017.
- **display** (Grouping Data Usage) = print that field on the **packing PDF for that order’s page**. It does not turn grouping off. A field can group and display.
- Plain process files are also **stock-ordering piles**. Packs vs Gildan T-shirts = **30-chain** (product type / brand), not package-type.
- Graph / Grouping Data **values are examples**, not a closed list — **except** Hashim #038 **category / subcategory / product type / product style** (closed pick-list `database/order-grouping-sorter/taxonomy_picklists.csv`). New products pick from that list; do not invent. Subcategory is PE `Sub-Category` (held on the list; not a 30-chain split). Logic = dimension + flag/threshold; missing Graph branch ≠ value off.
- **In-house manufacturer** = made in the warehouse (iron-on or sticker). **Plain cannot be in-house** → `unmatched`. Plain supply-method can be warehouse, on-demand, or later non-in-house values.
- **Supply Method** (catalog column on CL, Plain Database, Packs): CL `Warehouse Stock` = Fruit of the Loom men / women / kids **t-shirts in the locked colour lists only** (Department `Mens` / `Womens` / `Kids`; Ladies = Womens; exact `Colour` cell — Deep Navy is not Navy) **plus** Kids body styles **`C800T` / `C8030T`** in Black, Lemon Yellow, Light Blue, Light Pink, Red, Sports Grey, White. Not `C8020T`. Plain / Packs `Warehouse Stock` = all FOTL men / women / kids t-shirts (no colour list). `In House Manufacture` = Custom Label SKU or Gender Apparel contains `iron on` / `ironon` / `iron-on` / `sticker` (CL/printed only). `Supplier On Demand` = everything else. Do not reuse CL `Warehouse Stock`. Code: `shared/supply_method.py`. Locked and CL-filled 2026-09-23.
- **Printing Type** (CL only, printed split): `DTF` default; `Sublimation` = mugs. Mock leading `M##` → Mocks `Printing-Type` when DTF/Sublimation; else Category `Mugs` or Gender Apparel starts with `Mug` → Sublimation; else DTF. Do not fill Design Type. Code: `shared/printing_type.py`.
- **SKU match keys:** CL = **after first dash** (e.g. `77989LG-M-T-BLK-M` → `M-T-BLK-M`); **no dash → whole SKU** (`A515` → `A515`). Plain Database = **till last dash** (e.g. `1243-1` → `1243`); Packs = **whole SKU**. Entire-cell match only — no numeric stripping.
- **Plain vs printed** = finish gate (with SKU override): if Item SKU contains `plain` / `plainlg` → plain; else if CL DB matches after first dash (or whole SKU when there is no dash) → printed; else if Plain Database matches till last dash (or whole SKU) → plain; else if Packs Database matches whole SKU → plain; else `unmatched`.
- **SKU attribute source (catalog fields only):** Packs → CL → Plain Database (first hit). Unmatched if none hit when a field needs catalog data. A grouping **run** only reads the three catalogs. **Step 2 fill** may write CL, Plain Database, and Packs after fill/run.
- Mixed plain+printed in one order → whole order **printed** (printed-wins).
- **BTC Product Data** = the shared BTC supplier catalog. Live file: `database/shared/btc_product_data/BTC_Product_Data.csv` (`shared.paths.btc_product_data_path`). Same kind of sheet as **Uneek Product Data**.
- **Uneek Product Data** = the shared Uneek supplier catalog. Live file: `database/shared/uneek_product_data/Uneek_Product_Data.xlsx` (`shared.paths.uneek_product_data_path`). Same kind of sheet as **BTC Product Data** — supplier product rows, not warehouse Custom Label.
- **Absolute Product Data** = the shared Absolute Apparels supplier catalog. Live file: `database/shared/absolute_product_data/Absolute_Product_Data.xlsx` (`shared.paths.absolute_product_data_path`). Full wholesale price list; warehouse **only buys babysuits** from them (styles `C800T` / `C8020T` / `C8030T`).
- **Supplier Name** (catalog, grouping): canonical cells **`BTC Activewear`**, **`Uneek Clothing`**, **`Absolute Apparels`**. Absolute = babysuit styles only. Join: Absolute style token first, else BTC UID/SPC → BTC Activewear, Uneek Short Code/Product Code → Uneek Clothing. Packs short `BTC` normalizes to `BTC Activewear`. CL in-house (iron-on/sticker) stays blank. Filled 2026-09-09. Code: `shared/supplier_name.py`.
- **Plain Database** live file is `database/shared/plain/Plain Database.xlsx` (was under `purchase-order-generator/`).
- **Packs Database** live file is `database/shared/packs/Packs Database.xlsx`.
- **Hashim #038 taxonomy pick-list:** closed values for the four Areeb columns (category / product type / product style / department) plus PE subcategory. File: `database/order-grouping-sorter/taxonomy_picklists.csv`. Title Case. Product type has **no gender**. Product style is a named product/range, never a supplier code. When a product arrives, pick only from the list. Do not invent. Subcategory = PE `Sub-Category` (not a 30-chain split). **CL fill** snaps all four Areeb cells to the list. **Plain / Packs Areeb copy supplier product data** (BTC / Uneek) — do not refill those two from the warehouse pick-list. Code: `shared/taxonomy_picklist.py` + `shared/taxonomy_catalog.py`.
- **Areeb 30-chain columns** (distinct from PE `Category` / `Department`): `Category (Areeb)`, `Product Type (Areeb)`, `Product Style (Areeb)`, `Department (Areeb)` on CL, Plain Database, and Packs. Plain/Packs: BTC Department / Sub Department / Brand / Description; Uneek Category / Product Name / Full Description / Gender. Plain leftover (no UID / Short Code / SPC): Brand → Product Style, Description → Department, Category/Type from Description in BTC Department / Sub Department language (**no warehouse snap**). **Custom Label:** warehouse `cl_standard` from Gender Apparel only — never BTC, Uneek, PE, or Brand — then snap to the pick-list. **Department (Areeb) = gender only** (`Mens` / `Womens` / `Kids` / `Unisex` / `General`). Product Style is not CL Brand. Details: `.cursor/rules/custom-label-database/areeb-taxonomy.mdc`.
- **Order Grouping Sorter** = new app (folder `Order Grouping Sorter`), outside Packing. Reads ShipStation `awaiting_shipment` + the three catalogs. Writes one CSV per process into Packing Input. Testing: **`1st Shift`** every `--run`. Default CLI is dry-run until supervisor **run**.
- **All packing lists** (later, not built, 2026-09-17) = Order Packing List Generator only, including slips Purchase Order Generator still prints. Packing enrich today is CL-only (preflight Unmatched SKU = blank Gender Apparel; e.g. Packs `SET5722`). Later also Plain + Packs with sorter keys; catalog hit ≠ unmatched. Do **not** clone pack/plain SKUs into CL. PO later = EDI/stock only.
- **Missing-logo reprint** (Packing, locked 2026-09-17) = holding CSV has **no** process/item numbers. When logos exist, run that file in the **main packing app from Step 1**. Do not number the holding pile.
